WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.040
Just being at your side,

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:16.160
Gentles my hearts to the point of disbelief

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:25.570
I thought I heard the sound of your footsteps behind me,

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:35.720
I turned my head repeatedly, wishing you would appear...

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:41.740
...and then there you were

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:50.990
The beginning of a new love

00:00:51.310 --> 00:01:05.870
Is unknowingly, the beginning of our invisible love story

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:15.360
Hence, I shall never leave your side

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:24.540
I pledge to love you and only you

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.330
<i>It's OK, Chise...</i>

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.470
<i>I'll...kill you.</i>

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.940
Thank you, Shuji.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:41.570
I...

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:45.410
loved you, Shuji.

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:49.720
I'll never forget you. I really loved you.

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:54.460
- I'm fine. <i>- Enough.</i>

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:57.330
- You poor thing. <i>- I'll make it easy.</i>

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:59.750
- Thank you. <i>- You won't feel it.</i>

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:02.260
- Shuji, I... <i>- I'm going to...</i>

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.700
- love you. <i>- kill you.</i>

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:20.510
Chise, I'm home.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:24.580
Time for your pill.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:28.420
This is the last one.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.370
<i>I can't hear her voice anymore,</i>

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:42.770
<i>but, if I listen carefully,</i> <i>I can understand what she's saying.</i>

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:44.670
Turn around.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:50.680
Embarrassed? Dummy, after all this time!

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:09.270
Dummy, you're so pretty.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:11.800
Really pretty.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:14.840
Is this the end?

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:16.540
Damn...

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.070
I'm going nuts!

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:30.620
You know...

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:35.220
I just wish we had done it at least once.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.160
Dummy. You pervert.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:41.630
Sleep.

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:46.000
<i>I can hear her crying.</i>

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.540
<i>I can hear her living.</i>

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:54.500
<i>What's that I hear now?</i> <i>She's telling me, yes,</i>

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.040
<i>it must be a song...</i>

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:58.050
<i>I've heard before.</i>

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:05.320
"Love Song"

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:29.310
Chise...

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:31.250
No way...

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:33.020
Hey, Chise!

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:39.160
Dummy! It can be helped!

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:40.790
Damn it!

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.520
Cut it out!

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:45.150
Shuji...

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:50.320
I... I'm sorry this is kind of abrupt...

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:53.730
but, do you have someone you like?

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:55.910
Chise...

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:02.250
Um, I'm sorry... will you go out with me?

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:05.640
Uh... maybe we could...

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:09.150
study together sometime.

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:15.460
What's wrong, Shuji?

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:22.500
I'm sorry, it's too soon to call you by your first name.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:25.100
I hardly know you yet.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:28.760
Akemi said it's rude not to.

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:32.730
Maybe she was tricking me again.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:38.640
<i>She's warm. This really is Chise!</i>

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:45.050
You know, Chise, I loved you...

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:48.020
right from when you asked me out.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:53.990
You can use my first name. You're my girlfriend.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:59.240
We can study together, OK, Chise?

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.850
Show yourself! I know you're there!

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:20.890
I know you're there!

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:37.730
She's alive.

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:40.140
Chise's still alive.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:41.850
She's alive.

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:50.310
<i>I've committed a sin...</i>

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:56.190
<i>against this planet and</i> <i>all who live on it.</i>

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:57.490
<i>I...</i>

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:09.570
<i>wanted to save my girlfriend's life...</i>

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.900
<i>for my own selfish reasons.</i>

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:17.640
<i>By saving her life, I betrayed her.</i>

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:22.810
Can...Chise survive?

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:26.480
Probably.

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:34.260
But my rank is not high enough to know in what form.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:40.090
What lies ahead is either destruction or immortality.

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:45.090
Will Chise...survive?

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:47.410
She will.

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:53.820
No one can stop her, or kill her, now.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:59.690
She will be alive until the bitter end.

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:10.060
You told me to go back to my family.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:16.300
My wife and daughter died in the attack on Sapporo.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:21.970
My daughter was the same age as Chise.

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:29.080
It couldn't be helped. It's nobody's fault.

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:42.290
<i>"I wonder if I'll still be around</i> <i>when you read this."</i>

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:46.920
<i>"Are you eating right without me there?"</i>

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:49.790
<i>"Have you been bathing properly?"</i>

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:54.270
<i>She'd been keeping that diary</i> <i>since the day we ran off...</i>

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:58.400
<i>'til the day her medicine ran out.</i>

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:04.980
<i>"Shuji, I'm sorry I forced you</i> <i>to go out with me,"</i>

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:08.120
<i>"and run away with me, too."</i>

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:14.520
<i>"I'll never forget the three weeks</i> <i>we've spent as a married couple."</i>

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:22.320
<i>"Shuji... please, go back to your family."</i>

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:28.000
<i>"You just left them a note when</i> <i>we ran off together."</i>

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:30.370
<i>"They must be worried about you."</i>

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:36.180
<i>"If you manage to get back to our town,"</i>

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:39.580
<i>"I'd like you to do me one favor."</i>

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:54.460
Just a little farther to Chise's hometown.

00:10:55.270 --> 00:11:00.400
This is just earthquake damage, and there are lots of people.

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:05.130
Chise protects this town. I wonder what "Chise" actually is.

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:10.240
Hero or monster, guardian angel or destroyer?

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:11.980
Boring!

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:13.450
Sit down, now.

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:14.280
Sorry.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:17.420
It's like living in a myth.

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:21.520
For a scholar like me, it's exciting.

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:22.980
What's left here?

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:23.790
Huh?

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.220
What's in Chise's town?

00:11:27.430 --> 00:11:30.460
Nothing. There's nothing here!

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:33.700
It's just another boring small town...

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:37.710
nothing fun, with lots of hills...

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:40.210
and the army camped at the school.

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:44.270
Are you from here, by chance?

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:48.820
Then there is something for you here...

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.390
in Chise's town.

00:11:50.990 --> 00:11:53.420
In the Ainu language, "chise" means "house."

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:58.990
Oh father, really!

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:10.340
Shuji...

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:14.270
Father! Shuji's come home!

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:20.340
<i>As long as this town survives,</i> <i>I feel as if Chise's alive.</i>

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:26.720
<i>I can't see her, but it feels</i> <i>as if she's nearby.</i>

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:36.890
<i>"If you manage to get back to our town,"</i>

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:39.300
<i>"I'd like you to do me one favor."</i>

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:44.270
<i>"Go to the place where we first kissed."</i>

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:40.190
<i>It was a diary of everything</i> <i>since the day...</i>

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:42.830
<i>we started going out.</i>

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:50.170
<i>It was a record of how humanity</i> <i>was putting an end to itself.</i>

00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:55.480
<i>I heard Chise's unuttered voice</i> <i>of the soul...</i>

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:58.350
<i>about this tiny little planet...</i>

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:03.710
<i>and what had happened here</i> <i>that no one planned.</i>

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:09.560
<i>But who could stand that and</i> <i>not go crazy?!</i>

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:15.270
Damn it, don't run away from this!

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:25.440
<i>How long did it take me to read it all?</i>

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:30.510
<i>It talked about a school club, tests,</i>

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:35.910
<i>innocent and precious,</i> <i>describing the end of the world.</i>

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:48.410
Ch-Chise!

00:14:50.270 --> 00:14:51.860
Who are you?

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:54.800
Why are you here?

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:58.140
Why is Chise here?

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:00.510
It's me, Shuji!

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:02.000
"Shuji"...

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:10.150
Again, this stuff came out.

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:15.830
It came out when you were reading Chise's diary.

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:18.530
This liquid, what is it?

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:23.730
Chise was programmed to come here when you do.

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:25.600
Why is that?

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:28.360
Chise was waiting for you!

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:35.780
Your pulse, respiration and adrenalin levels were all elevated.

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:37.210
Chise's too.

00:15:37.770 --> 00:15:41.650
And I received much data that did not compute.

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:44.670
Many emotive thoughts,

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:50.830
like "sadness," "suffering," "grief," "crying," "pity"...

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:53.590
then, finally...

00:15:54.400 --> 00:15:59.200
"I'm glad you know. I've been so sad!"

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:01.160
Why this pain?

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:02.410
What's happening?

00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:06.910
Don't touch me. I'll kill you.

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:14.650
You put saliva in Chise's mouth.

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:18.280
Why? Why did you do that?

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:20.450
Because I'm your boyfriend!

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:22.750
And you're my girlfriend!

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:27.560
Is that so? Does that explain everything?

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:29.290
That's right!

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:34.330
Then, this strong emotion that I can't process,

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:36.810
does it explain that, too?

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:39.910
"I want to have Shuji's baby."

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:45.910
That thought's always been in Chise's old brain,

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:50.210
but it's grown stronger as she's become less human.

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:56.920
She kept it hidden away for fear she'd die of shame,

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:00.720
and that it would terrify you.

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:02.660
Chise.

00:17:04.740 --> 00:17:09.440
Why are you crying? Chise can't be killed by shame.

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:13.840
Why would you be afraid of a baby? Why?

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:18.110
You want to create another human being with me? Dummy!

00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:22.380
My face is hot...my heart is pounding...

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:25.720
Is this what shame is?

00:17:26.390 --> 00:17:31.020
What is this "reproduction"? Is it that scary?

00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:33.190
No, it's not, dummy.

00:17:34.730 --> 00:17:38.930
Let's do it, Chise. It's something we can do together.

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:42.960
There's really nothing to be scared of.

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:44.270
OK?

00:17:46.780 --> 00:17:48.970
Um... uh...

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:51.410
Don't cry!

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:54.510
Here, touch my breasts.

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:58.680
Uh, are we really going to?

00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:02.530
I don't have Chise's old body, anymore.

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:06.650
I have reproductive organs, but they're not necessary--

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:07.950
Will you be quiet?

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:13.630
And I don't have the feelings that go with reproductive acts, so...

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:18.370
and if I get too excited, I might kill you!

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:20.060
Be quiet!

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:36.480
It broke off. Maybe I shouldn't have tried to make myself

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:38.830
into the old Chise.

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:41.190
"The old Chise"?

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:45.830
The molecules come apart if I move wrong.

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:47.150
I'll fix it.

00:18:50.740 --> 00:18:54.970
Not in the mood anymore? Well, maybe it's for the best.

00:18:55.210 --> 00:18:59.380
I don't feel anything anyway.

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:03.460
Nothing's connected down there.

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:08.290
Reproductive organs are useless anyway.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:12.850
Dummy! Maybe useless to a weapon, but still...

00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:18.290
Dummy, not just for weapons. This planet won't need them either.

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:20.840
I see!

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:27.340
When you re-formed your body, you made your breasts bigger, Chise.

00:19:27.510 --> 00:19:30.450
No way! I did not!

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:32.850
I know...

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:34.250
Shuji...

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:37.380
You haven't grown up at all.

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:39.290
I'm sorry!

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:42.860
What's that, "I'm sorry"?

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:45.390
I remember...

00:19:46.510 --> 00:19:47.480
"I'm sorry"?

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:51.000
Shuji, what is it?

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:52.730
"I'm sorry."

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:56.850
"I'm sorry", why does that make my chest tight?

00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:59.540
Dummy, I told you not to say "sorry."

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:02.840
I'm sorry.

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:04.650
Shuji...

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:10.410
Why do I feel embarrassed?

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:13.110
No, I can't stop it.

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:15.080
Can I kill you?

00:20:15.490 --> 00:20:18.620
I need to kill someone!

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:22.890
I can't stop myself, I'm a weapon!

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:26.430
Shuji don't! I'm going to break down!

00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:28.340
I can't stop it!

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:33.940
Dummy! I want to keep living!

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:37.310
I don't want to die!

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:41.230
No one does!

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:48.420
Shuji...

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:53.760
I've been hearing it,

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:56.160
your heartbeat.

00:20:56.930 --> 00:21:01.270
It's saying "I want to live, I want to live."

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:05.270
It always beats like this when I'm with you!

00:21:06.110 --> 00:21:09.510
It's been beating like this since that first day!

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:13.710
War or no war, however the world changes,

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:16.420
even if it ends,

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:21.890
when I'm with you, it always sounds the same.

00:21:23.660 --> 00:21:24.490
Oh, I hear it.

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:26.830
Listen, Chise.

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:29.620
It's not much,

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:33.330
but it's something we left on this planet!

00:21:33.870 --> 00:21:34.860
Shuji...

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:37.360
I can feel you.

00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:39.500
Your heart's pounding.

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:43.410
That means you love me!

00:21:44.980 --> 00:21:45.970
You're crying.

00:21:48.020 --> 00:21:48.990
I'm sorry.

00:21:49.520 --> 00:21:51.250
Don't cry, now.

00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:54.020
I'll start crying, too.

00:21:55.490 --> 00:21:57.960
Shuji, your heart's pounding.

00:21:58.800 --> 00:22:00.590
Shuji, I can feel it.

00:22:02.220 --> 00:22:03.930
<i>Again and again,</i>

00:22:03.990 --> 00:22:07.940
<i>we sought out each other,</i> <i>in shared ecstasy...</i>

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:13.610
<i>in a barren coupling born</i> <i>only of human desire.</i>

00:22:14.970 --> 00:22:18.170
<i>Each time, Chise said,</i> <i>"I'm sorry" and cried.</i>

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:24.210
<i>Again and again she cried,</i> <i>as if feeling the joy of living...</i>

00:22:24.790 --> 00:22:27.120
<i>were a sin.</i>

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:43.420
A rift opened up upon my heart

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:49.990
And I went through the night sleepless, sighing constantly

00:22:50.670 --> 00:22:59.340
Before I realize, it's turned to morning

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:08.660
I want to hear your voice

00:23:09.180 --> 00:23:13.250
I want to feel your warmth

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:19.460
Thoughts of you well up within me

00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:25.310
And my tears begin to overflow

00:23:25.320 --> 00:23:36.570
Goodbye my beloved, I am still unable to forget about you

00:23:36.730 --> 00:23:46.740
Having all of this end with just a single word of goodbye

00:23:47.240 --> 00:23:51.570
Fills me with sorrow

00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:02.950
Is this how the world's going to end?

00:24:03.820 --> 00:24:07.590
Chise, I'll wait for you here. I promise... I'll be here.

00:24:08.320 --> 00:24:14.020
SAIKANO, Final Episode: "And We Will Love"
